            <ArticleTitle>[Are unknown ciliates responsible for uncharacteristic pains in the lower abdomen (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1271-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is reported about unknown cells, looking like ciliates, found in the Douglas exudate in women with uncharacteristic pains in the lower abdomen. These self-moving cells were found in 10 out of 48 patients. The clinical results are discussed. There is a possibility that these cells are responsible as well for the uncharacteristic pains in the abdomen as perhaps for the infertility of the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
